      "writtenOn": "2024-09-12T20:58:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It should be fine for all NDK libraries (which are also LL-NDK libraries, the only ones this matters for). LL-NDK has always implicitly included NDK APIs, using \u002736\u0027 would mean that we have the same behavior here that we\u0027ve always had for the LL-NDK/NDK in Android.\n\nLeaving it 35 means that the trend set by Trunk Stable, which allows for LL-NDK and NDK APIs to be defined at separate times, to continue moving forward. The reason the LL-NDK had to lag behind for 202404/34 was because the LL-NDK API was frozen 1 quarter earlier last year.\n\nLeaving it as 35 is also the most flexible choice possible here, which is why I put it in the CL itself. It\u0027s my preference beacuse:\n- pro: makes Android V start a trend, rather than being special\n- pro: allows us to specify LL-NDK/NDK membership independently this year\n- con: requires two lines of .txt for an API to be included in 202404 and 36",
